1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,327
What if every promise you heard left

2
00:00:03,347 --> 00:00:04,347
a thread?

3
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:06,054
A real one.

4
00:00:06,190 --> 00:00:06,807
Glowing.

5
00:00:06,827 --> 00:00:09,532
Tied from their wrist to your heart.

6
00:00:10,868 --> 00:00:13,157
Keep the promise, and it lights up

7
00:00:13,176 --> 00:00:14,336
like a firework.

8
00:00:14,442 --> 00:00:15,442
Break it

9
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:17,170
and it hangs there.

10
00:00:17,289 --> 00:00:17,719
Grey.

11
00:00:17,739 --> 00:00:19,367
For everyone to see.

12
00:00:19,484 --> 00:00:19,916
Well.

13
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:21,268
For YOU to see.

14
00:00:24,986 --> 00:00:26,015
You wake up.

15
00:00:26,125 --> 00:00:28,684
Your alarm promises, "five more minutes."

16
00:00:29,385 --> 00:00:31,507
The thread snaps grey before you even

17
00:00:31,527 --> 00:00:32,527
sit up.

18
00:00:32,865 --> 00:00:36,556
Downstairs, Mom says, "I'll drive you today."

19
00:00:36,576 --> 00:00:37,171
Gold.

20
00:00:37,192 --> 00:00:37,786
Thick.

21
00:00:37,807 --> 00:00:39,118
Already glowing.

22
00:00:39,978 --> 00:00:42,282
Your little brother promises he'll "clean

23
00:00:42,302 --> 00:00:43,694
his room THIS time."

24
00:00:44,393 --> 00:00:46,834
His wrist is a mess.

25
00:00:47,906 --> 00:00:49,601
The rules are simple.

26
00:00:49,725 --> 00:00:51,972
Every promise makes a thread.

27
00:00:52,094 --> 00:00:53,737
Big promises, thick threads.

28
00:00:53,859 --> 00:00:55,698
Kept ones turn to light.

29
00:00:55,822 --> 00:00:58,109
Broken ones turn grey and drag.

30
00:00:58,932 --> 00:01:00,994
The bus driver: "I'll wait for you!"

31
00:01:01,994 --> 00:01:04,984
A billboard promises "your best summer ever."

32
00:01:05,004 --> 00:01:07,596
The thread goes up into the sky,

33
00:01:07,646 --> 00:01:08,712
and just ends.

34
00:01:09,737 --> 00:01:12,674
By lunch, you learn the first secret.

35
00:01:12,814 --> 00:01:14,742
Most promises aren't lies.

36
00:01:14,882 --> 00:01:16,299
People just forget.

37
00:01:20,239 --> 00:01:22,540
At school, it's like seeing the future.

38
00:01:23,341 --> 00:01:25,444
"I'll pay you back Friday." Thin.

39
00:01:25,561 --> 00:01:26,561
Already sagging.

40
00:01:26,643 --> 00:01:28,076
You keep your money.

41
00:01:28,894 --> 00:01:29,329
Ms.

42
00:01:29,349 --> 00:01:32,115
Bell: "I'll grade them by Monday." Twenty-eight

43
00:01:32,135 --> 00:01:34,850
threads, one to every desk, all still

44
00:01:34,870 --> 00:01:35,870
gold.

45
00:01:36,025 --> 00:01:37,025
She means it.

46
00:01:37,078 --> 00:01:38,114
She's just tired.

47
00:01:39,025 --> 00:01:41,314
At casino night, a kid swears he'll

48
00:01:41,334 --> 00:01:43,668
"split the winnings." The thread is already

49
00:01:43,688 --> 00:01:45,745
grey before the cards are dealt.

50
00:01:46,551 --> 00:01:48,242
You stop trusting words.

51
00:01:48,381 --> 00:01:50,072
You start trusting threads.

52
00:01:51,212 --> 00:01:51,989
Group projects?

53
00:01:52,009 --> 00:01:53,602
You pick the gold ones.

54
00:01:53,709 --> 00:01:54,185
Dates?

55
00:01:54,204 --> 00:01:54,981
Gold ones.

56
00:01:55,001 --> 00:01:56,001
Friends?

57
00:01:57,009 --> 00:01:59,650
For about a week, your life is

58
00:01:59,670 --> 00:02:01,552
perfectly organised by light.

59
00:02:05,474 --> 00:02:07,239
Then you notice Maya.

60
00:02:08,075 --> 00:02:09,906
There's a thread between you.

61
00:02:10,021 --> 00:02:10,444
Old.

62
00:02:10,465 --> 00:02:12,295
From a long time ago.

63
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:15,305
"I'll always save you a seat." You

64
00:02:15,325 --> 00:02:16,664
remember her saying it.

65
00:02:16,768 --> 00:02:17,814
In second grade.

66
00:02:18,617 --> 00:02:19,776
It's still there.

67
00:02:19,901 --> 00:02:20,709
Still gold.

68
00:02:20,729 --> 00:02:21,391
Barely.

69
00:02:21,412 --> 00:02:23,480
Because she still saves it.

70
00:02:23,604 --> 00:02:24,604
Every day.

71
00:02:24,639 --> 00:02:26,604
And you never sit there.

72
00:02:28,128 --> 00:02:30,638
You start seeing it everywhere.

73
00:02:30,781 --> 00:02:31,716
Not lies.

74
00:02:31,736 --> 00:02:32,736
Just waiting.

75
00:02:34,013 --> 00:02:35,862
Late at night, you find Dad at

76
00:02:35,883 --> 00:02:36,883
the kitchen table.

77
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:39,044
He has one thread.

78
00:02:39,164 --> 00:02:39,709
One.

79
00:02:39,729 --> 00:02:41,198
Thick as a rope.

80
00:02:41,318 --> 00:02:41,762
Gold.

81
00:02:41,782 --> 00:02:44,137
Going to every one of you.

82
00:02:45,257 --> 00:02:46,990
You ask him what he promised.

83
00:02:47,082 --> 00:02:47,681
He laughs.

84
00:02:47,701 --> 00:02:49,433
"That I'd take care of you."

85
00:02:50,133 --> 00:02:51,788
He never said it out loud.

86
00:02:51,879 --> 00:02:52,555
Not once.

87
00:02:52,575 --> 00:02:54,471
And it's the brightest thread in the

88
00:02:54,491 --> 00:02:55,491
house.

89
00:02:56,324 --> 00:02:58,152
That night, you can't sleep.

90
00:03:01,578 --> 00:03:03,721
You go to the bathroom, turn on

91
00:03:03,741 --> 00:03:05,865
the light and look in the mirror.

92
00:03:06,668 --> 00:03:08,340
You never thought to look at your

93
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,360
OWN wrist.

94
00:03:09,806 --> 00:03:10,981
There are hundreds.

95
00:03:13,288 --> 00:03:15,467
"I'll start tomorrow." "I'll call Grandma."

96
00:03:15,487 --> 00:03:17,798
"I'll be nicer to Leo." "I'll text

97
00:03:17,818 --> 00:03:18,818
you back."

98
00:03:19,457 --> 00:03:21,048
Most of them are grey.

99
00:03:21,153 --> 00:03:23,324
And they all lead to people you

100
00:03:23,344 --> 00:03:24,344
love.

101
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:26,987
But one is older than all the

102
00:03:27,008 --> 00:03:28,008
others.

103
00:03:28,134 --> 00:03:29,134
You follow it.

104
00:03:30,276 --> 00:03:31,739
It leads to YOU.

105
00:03:31,867 --> 00:03:33,072
Seven years old.

106
00:03:33,901 --> 00:03:35,085
I'll be brave.

107
00:03:36,611 --> 00:03:38,498
Promises to yourself count too.

108
00:03:38,611 --> 00:03:40,631
You just never see them break.

109
00:03:45,943 --> 00:03:47,877
So the next morning, you keep one.

110
00:03:48,665 --> 00:03:49,817
Just one.

111
00:03:49,995 --> 00:03:50,995
Small.

112
00:03:51,574 --> 00:03:53,599
You sit in the seat Maya saves.

113
00:03:54,399 --> 00:03:57,082
And the thread between you doesn't snap.

114
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:58,756
It ignites.

115
00:04:01,512 --> 00:04:02,740
You call Grandma.

116
00:04:02,872 --> 00:04:03,355
Gold.

117
00:04:03,376 --> 00:04:05,614
You help Leo clean his room.

118
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:08,518
He's so shocked, HIS thread bursts too.

119
00:04:09,449 --> 00:04:11,704
Your wrist doesn't get lighter overnight.

120
00:04:11,818 --> 00:04:13,225
But it gets brighter.

121
00:04:14,341 --> 00:04:15,478
And that oldest thread?

122
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:16,786
You're working on it.

123
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:18,471
So.

124
00:04:18,490 --> 00:04:21,048
If you could see every promise you've

125
00:04:21,067 --> 00:04:22,067
made

126
00:04:22,161 --> 00:04:23,961
how many would still be waiting?
